01:09:31,304 --> 01:09:37,304
Southpaw is a 2015 American sports drama film directed by Antoine Fuqua, written by Kurt
Sutter and starring Jake Gyllenhaal, Forest Whitaker and Rachel McAdams.

14
01:14:52,173 --> 01:14:58,173
The film follows a boxer who sets out to get his life back on track after losing his wife
to gun violence and later his young daughter to child protective services.

15
01:20:13,043 --> 01:20:19,043
The film was released on July 24, 2015, by The Weinstein Company.

16
01:25:33,913 --> 01:25:39,913
The film received mixed reviews from critics, while Gyllenhaal and
Oona Laurence's performances received positive reviews.

17
01:30:54,782 --> 01:31:00,782
The film grossed $94.2 million worldwide against a
production budget of $30 million.

18
01:36:15,652 --> 01:36:21,652
The film is set in New York City, but it was filmed in
Pittsburgh and the nearby town of Indiana, Pennsylvania.

19
01:41:36,521 --> 01:41:42,521
The film marked one of the last films to be scored by James Horner and the first of three posthumous
releases to feature his music (the other two being The 33 and The Magnificent Seven).

20
01:46:57,391 --> 01:47:03,391
The film and the film's soundtrack album are dedicated to his memory.

21
01:52:18,260 --> 01:52:24,260
The film explores themes of sports, fighter, tragedy, death, boxing.

22
01:57:39,130 --> 01:57:45,130
The tone is emotional.
